● Now it uses the proper HEADLESS approach:

  1. sway_dual_stack_enable:
    - Stacks physical DSI outputs vertically (DSI-2@0,0 + DSI-1@0,480)
    - Creates HEADLESS-1 at 640x960 via swaymsg create_output
    - Sets custom mode 640x960 on the headless output
    - Moves workspace to HEADLESS — apps fullscreen to the single 640x960 surface naturally
    - Touch calibration updated for stacked layout
  2. sway_dual_stack_disable:
    - Moves workspace back to primary physical output
    - Destroys HEADLESS via swaymsg output HEADLESS-1 unplug
    - Powers off secondary, resets touch

  Apps see one unified 640x960 output, not two 640x480 outputs. No floating enable, fullscreen disable, resize set hacks needed.


